          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If a note says \"use additional code\", is that optional?",
          "answer": "The retrieved passages don't settle whether \"use additional code\" is mandatory, so I can't give you a firm yes or no from them.\n\nWhat they do say:\n\n- **Code structure and conventions** (coding-icd10-cm-code-structure-and-conventions) describes \"code first\" and \"use additional code\" as a pair that fixes sequencing. The underlying condition is reported before its manifestation. It does not say whether the second code can be skipped.\n- **Chapter 18 symptoms** (coding-icd10-chapter-18-symptoms) says a symptom code is normally dropped once a diagnosis is documented. The exception is a symptom that is not routinely associated with that diagnosis, which is reported in addition because it adds information. This is the closest the corpus comes to a case where an additional code is needed, but it is not a rule about the instruction itself.\n- **Asthma (J45)** and **COPD (J44)** notes describe tobacco codes as added alongside the main code. They do not say whether that addition is compulsory.\n\nThe guidance I searched does not cover the official ICD-10-CM Official Guidelines for Coding and Reporting, which are the authoritative source for this question. Check that document, or ask a certified coder or your facility's coding policy, for a definitive answer.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
